The plate is a square plate about 26 cm across the diagonal, so the side is roughly 24 cm. The corn piece has a diameter of about 4 cm, which is 100 px out of about 420 px for the plate diagonal. It looks like a short cob segment about 2.5 cm tall, probably a cut section of boiled corn on the cob.

Estimated volume is π × 2² × 2.5 ≈ 31 cm³. The cob core takes up some of that, so the edible weight is about 30 g. Boiled corn on the cob is about 95 kcal per 100 g, or around 100 with the cob.

